## Scope note (read before the table)

`docs/context/methodology.md` keeps React component verification manual, and
ADR-0008 states explicitly that test-first "does not mean writing React
component tests first". This phase's testable surface is therefore exactly
the two pure `src/shared/` modules the plan creates (Task 1 `app-route.ts`,
Task 2 `google-settings.ts`) plus the one Worker route change (Task 9,
`oauth-callback.ts`'s success leg). `SettingsScreen.tsx`, `GoogleConnectionCard.tsx`,
`useRoute.ts`, `TodayHeader.tsx` and `App.tsx` are React/browser-API glue,
verified on the device per the plan's own Notes — no test file is authored
for them, and none of the outcomes below treats that absence as a gap.

Several PRD ACs this phase's plan cites (AC-1, AC-4, AC-15) already have full
SERVER-side coverage from phase 2/3, unaffected by this phase (no route file
is in this phase's `## Files to Change`). Where the plan adds a genuine new
CLIENT-side property to one of those ACs (a delta), the outcome below is
`NEW_TEST_REQUIRED` for that delta, with the pre-existing coverage cited in
the new test's own header comment rather than duplicated.

