## Correction round (dispute-driven revision, attempt 2)

**Trigger:** the `/relay-implement` attempt on this plan produced a
`TEST_CONTRACT_DISPUTE` (`PRPs/reports/google-calendar-read/phase-5/attempts/1/record.json`):
Level 2 (`npm test`) reported 3 failing (of the 3 disputed assertions) while
the 21 new phase-5 unit tests — Tasks 1–2, `test/app-route.test.ts` /
`test/google-settings.test.ts` — all passed. The Implementer's diff itself
was not in question: `src/worker/routes/oauth-callback.ts` returns
`c.redirect(destination.toString(), 302)` exactly as Task 9 specifies.

**Arbitration:** `DISPUTE_UPHELD_TEST_WRONG`
(`PRPs/reports/google-calendar-read/phase-5/halt.json`). Evidence: `SELF: Fetcher`
is documented `@deprecated` in `node_modules/@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers/types/cloudflare-test.d.ts`
in favour of `exports.default.fetch()`, which auto-follows redirects exactly
like global `fetch()`; `src/worker/index.ts` has no `/settings` route;
`wrangler.jsonc`'s `assets.run_worker_first` is exactly `["/api/*", "/oauth/*"]`,
deliberately excluding `/settings`; and a real browser follows the identical
302 into the SPA shell via `not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` —
production behaviour is correct, and only the test harness's observation was
wrong.

**Correction applied this session — exactly three assertions, two files,
nothing else:**

- `test/oauth-callback-redirect.test.ts` — the two disputed cases — added
  `redirect: "manual"` to the `exports.default.fetch()` call in each, so the
  raw 3xx response is observed instead of the harness's auto-followed 404.
  No assertion was loosened, removed, or skipped; the status-range and
  Location-resolution checks are unchanged from what the approved suite
  already asserted.
- `test/oauth-callback.test.ts` — the pre-existing case "exchanges the code
  and stores the refresh token" — same fix, same reasoning (collateral
  damage from the identical auto-follow). Its sibling "never echoes the
  refresh token back in the response body" (`:202-208`) was read and
  confirmed to need no change, per the reasoning in the ledger row above, and
  was left untouched.

**Not touched, by design:** no file under `src/` (the implementation is
arbitrated as correct and the working tree holds it uncommitted); no new test
file created; no test besides the three named above; no `git` history-
mutating command (stash/checkout/clean/reset/commit) was run.

